                    briefing_text_r1:       `The president's plan promises <strong>€1.3bn</strong> — €660M of growth on the €640M base — but <strong>62% of that growth rides on two unsigned EV contracts</strong>, in a division whose forecasts have averaged <em>±22% error</em>. Resist the instinct to verdict early. Decompose the revenue bridge into committed, probable and speculative; take the <strong>outside view</strong> on the optimism the ±22% record signals; and name the two sandbagged cost centres and the over-stretched top-line by evidence, not blame. The CFO's fear is the last division that hit every slide and missed reality by 30%.`,
